{
  "name": "Midnight",
  "type": "weapon",
  "img": "worlds/the-broken-heart-of-greenrest/assets/icons/midnight-longsword-v2.png",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>The blade that was First Light. The rose-gold has run to ink; the steel drinks the candlelight and gives none of it back. It is not cold. It is simply without dawn.</em></p><p>Consecrated once to the Morninglord and surrendered in a sunless temple, this longsword now belongs to the Lady of Loss. The warmth left it the way a door closes somewhere far off — no thunderclap, no wrath: withdrawal. Its bearer knows the sword's name the way he knows his own reflection.</p><p>You gain a <strong>+2 bonus</strong> to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon, and a hit deals an extra <strong>1d8 Necrotic damage</strong>.</p><p><strong>Death Armor.</strong> Once per day, the bearer may cast <em>Death Armor</em> from the sword (no spell slot). This use recovers at dawn.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
